citeturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Agelos Georgakopoulos ... In this note we prove the conjecture of \\citeHaWiWi that every bipartite multigraph with integer edge delays admits an edge colouring with $d+1$ colours in the special case where $d=3$. ... The two values are not very far from each other, and so cover cost might be a useful tool in the study of cover time.\n\nPDF\n\nIn this note we prove the conjecture of \\citeHaWiWi that every bipartite multigraph with integer edge delays admits an edge colouring with $d+1$ colours in the special case where $d=3$. A connection to the Brualdi-Ryser-Stein conjecture is discussed.\n\n  * A Tractable Variant of Cover Time\n\nAgelos Georgakopoulos\n\nJun 29 2012 math.CO cs.DM arXiv:1206.6605v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1206.6605, author = {Agelos Georgakopoulos}, title = {{A} {T}ractable {V}ariant of {C}over {T}ime}, year = {2012}, eprint = {1206.6605}, note = {arXiv:1206.6605v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe introduce a variant of the cover time of a graph, called cover cost, in which the cost of a step is proportional to the number of yet uncovered vertices. It turns out that cover cost is more tractable than cover time; we provide an $O(n^4)$ algorithm for its computation, as well as some explicit formulae. The two values are not very far from each other, and so cover cost might be a useful tool in the study of cover time.\n\n  * The Liouville and the intersection properties are equivalent for planar graphs\n\nItai Benjamini, Nicolas Curien, Agelos Georgakopoulos\n\nMar 20 2012 math.PR arXiv:1203.4002v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1203.4002, author = {Itai Benjamini and Nicolas Curien and Agelos Georgakopoulos}, title = {{T}he {L}iouville and the intersection properties are equivalent for planar graphs}, year = {2012}, eprint = {1203.4002}, note = {arXiv:1203.4002v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nIt is shown that if a planar graph admits no non-constant bounded harmonic functions then the trajectories of two independent simple random walks intersect almost surely.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Tractable Variant of Cover Time (https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=a1897a9b3ee8a404cfcdf9d3d864afb22c967874&repid=rep1&type=pdf)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; would allow us to use cover cost in order to obtain bounds on cover time. ... Conjecture 5.4. ... Georgakopoulos and S.\nProblem 5.3. Which rooted graph on n vertices minimises ccr(G)?\nWhich\nmaximises it?\nIt would be very interesting to obtain bounds on ccr(G)/CTr(G), for this\nwould allow us to use cover cost in order to obtain bounds on cover time. The\nfollowing two problems are motivated by this.\nConjecture 5.4. The path on n vertices rooted at an endpoint maximises\nccr(G)/CTr(G) over all rooted graphs G on n vertices.\nProblem 5.5. Is there a graph G for which ccr(G)/CTr(G) < 1/H(|V (G)|−1)\nwhere Hn ≈ln n is the nth harmonic number?\nWhich graph on n vertices\nminimises ccr(G)/CTr(G)?\nAcknowledgements\nI am very grateful to Itai Benjamini, Erol Pekoz, and Peter Winkler for their\naforementioned suggestions and other valuable discussions.\nReferences\n[AF]\nD.J.\nAldous\nand\nJ.\nFill,\nReversible\nmarkov\nchains\nand\nrandom\nwalks\non\ngraphs,\nMonograph\nin\npreparation.\nhttp://www.stat.berkeley.edu/˜aldous/RWG/book.html.\n[AKL+79] R. Aleliunas, R. Karp, R. Lipton, L. Lov´asz, and C. Rackoﬀ, Ran-\ndom walks, universal traversal sequences, and the complexity of maze\ntraversal, Proc. 20th IEEE Symp. Found. Computer Science (1979),\n218–233.\n[Bro90]\nA. Broder, Universal sequences and graph cover times; a short sur-\nvey, Sequences (Naples/Positano, 1988) Springer, New York (1990),\n109–122.\n[BW90]\nG. R. Brightwell and P. Winkler, Extremal cover time for random\nwalks on trees, J. Graph Theory 14 (1990), no. 5, 547–554.\n[DLP]\nJ. Ding, J.R. Lee, an